From 8386d76fa22a9a5e541734495879ebf3b76aaaed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:27:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] plugins: add an oFono plugin

The oFono plugin was removed in 2021, and with it support for every
phone that runs oFono instead of ModemManager. Add it back, written for
GDBus and the current service API:

- it talks to oFono on the system bus, whichever bus mmsd-tng is on;
- it follows every modem oFono has and serves the one MMS service on
  the first that has a SIM with a known IMSI, a connection manager and
  push notifications, which on a dual SIM phone need not be the first
  modem. It sets the country code and own number from that SIM. When
  the modem stops qualifying or goes away, the next one that qualifies
  takes over;
- it registers a push notification agent on that modem only, and
  accepts pushes only from oFono's unique name, since anyone on the
  system bus could otherwise hand mmsd-tng a notification pointing at
  any URL;
- it takes the MMSC, the proxy and the IPv4 and IPv6 DNS servers from
  oFono's MMS context, brings the context up when the service asks for
  the bearer, and takes it down when the service lets go of it, or when
  the modem is let go of, but only if it brought it up itself;
- when the MMS context has the same APN as the internet context, which
  modems generally refuse to activate a second time, it carries MMS
  over the internet context instead, as FuriLabs' mmsd4ofono does;
- it only tells the service the bearer is up when the interface or
  proxy changed, because every such call restarts the transfer.

Build it with -Dofono=true.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
